# Typography: hyphens only

Always use a plain hyphen `-` (U+002D). Never use em dash `—` (U+2014) or en dash `–` (U+2013).

## Spacing

When a hyphen separates phrases or clauses, always put a space on both sides: ` - `

```
// BAD
"Arabkir Heights- Yerevan"
"developers- transparent pricing"

// GOOD
"Arabkir Heights - Yerevan"
"developers - transparent pricing"
```

Empty or missing values use a single hyphen with no spaces: `"-"`.

## Applies to

- User-facing copy in translations (`content/`, `lib/translations-*.ts`)
- UI strings, labels, alt text, meta titles, and SEO titles
- Comments and documentation when separating clauses or list items

## Examples

```
// BAD
"CASA GROUP — new apartments in Yerevan"
"Monthly payment —"

// GOOD
"CASA GROUP - new apartments in Yerevan"
"Monthly payment -"
emptyLabel = "-"
```

Do not change hyphens inside code identifiers, CSS classes, slugs, URLs, or compound words (e.g. `next-intl`, `line-clamp-3`, `Arabkir Heights-ը`).
